WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.760
"The Best Diet for Fatty
Liver Disease Treatment"

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:14.800
Nonalcoholic fatty liver
disease is now the most frequent

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.000
chronic liver disease thanks,
in part, to our epidemic

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.440
of obesity, now even seen in children.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:24.240
As many as nearly 70 to
80% of obese children

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.360
may have fatty liver disease.
Why do we care?

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.360
Because a fatty liver can
progress into fatty hepatitis,

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.680
which can cause scarring
and liver cirrhosis,

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.400
which is bad enough
without also causing you

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:40.000
to develop liver cancer, too.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.640
Okay, so what’s the source of the
liver fat in fatty liver disease?

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:48.720
There are three main sources:
the excess sugar in our diet,

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:52.720
excess fat in our diet,
and the fat spilling over

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:55.680
from your own excess body fat.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.880
How do we know excess
dietary sugar is bad?

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:01.935
Because it’s been put to the test.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.560
If you randomize teens with
fatty liver disease to a diet

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:08.320
low in free sugars (meaning
added sugar and sugary beverages),

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:11.840
they experience a significant
improvement within eight weeks.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.640
Given this new data, a liver
journal editorial read,

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.200
“[a] strong argument can
be made that we are beyond

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.840
any period of uncertainty
about the harmful effects

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:23.040
of excess sugar consumption
and that we must now act ...

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:28.080
to inform the public of the health
risks of eating too much sugar.”

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:31.360
How do we know excess
dietary fat is bad?

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:33.920
Because it’s been put to the test.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.320
Randomize people to the
same low-calorie diet,

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:39.440
but one that’s low-fat
versus one that’s high-fat,

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:42.160
and within just two
weeks the low-fat diet

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:44.960
decreased liver fat by 20%,
whereas the same number

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:49.920
of calories on a high-fat
diet increased liver fat by 35%!

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.360
On the low-fat diet, insulin
levels went down about 15%,

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:57.600
and on the high-fat diet,
insulin levels went up about 15%.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.880
Low-carb and ketogenic diet
advocates are always talking

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:03.680
about how you have to eat
more fat and less carbs

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:06.480
to keep your insulin levels down,
but the exact opposite

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:09.520
happens when it’s
actually put to the test.

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:13.200
Even a single high-fat meal
not only increases liver fat

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.200
but also insulin resistance.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:18.880
Within four hours, your whole-
body insulin sensitivity

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:22.400
can drop by 25%; so, your
body has to pump out

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.160
that much more insulin.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.560
As the accompanying editorial put it,

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:30.880
a single fat dose packs a punch.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:33.760
So, to help prevent or
treat fatty liver disease,

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:37.857
patients should limit or
avoid eating fat-rich foods.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:40.960
While more long-term clinical
trials are always needed,

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:43.760
based on current evidence,
we would recommend a diet

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:46.720
low in fat, notably
saturated fat, so low in meat,

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:52.000
dairy, and junk, and low in
reﬁned carbs, notably soda.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.960
Saturated fat is not only
more metabolically harmful

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:58.320
for the human liver than
unsaturated fat, saturated fat

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.520
is more harmful than straight sugar.

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:03.760
If you overfeed people
with 1,000 calories

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:06.080
of saturated fat
(like cheese and coconut oil),

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.880
unsaturated fat (like nuts and olive oil),

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:12.800
or sugar (like soda and candy),
overeating 1,000 calories a day

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:15.920
of anything isn’t good for you,
but the saturated fat

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:19.040
increased liver fat 55%,
significantly more than

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:24.000
the unsaturated fats, with
the candy coming in in-between.

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:27.120
So, in terms of weight loss,
although beneﬁcial,

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.720
certain diets can actually
cause or exacerbate this disease,

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:33.840
such as very low-carbohydrate,
high-fat diets,

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:36.400
whereas those eating
healthy plant-based diets

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:39.120
may lower the risk of fatty liver disease.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:41.760
For example, the consumption
of legumes (beans, split peas,

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.560
chickpeas, and lentils) is
associated with a lower risk

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:50.234
of fatty liver, up to 65%
lower odds eating more beans.

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:53.120
Now, in this study, they weren’t
looking at people eating

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:56.240
strictly plant-based diets,
just more or less so.

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:57.840
It’s harder to study those eating

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.560
completely meat-free diets
since they currently represent

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:02.640
just a small segment
of the U.S. population.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:05.840
But what about Americans
of Indian descent?

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:08.560
Those originating from the
Indian subcontinent are one

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:11.440
of the fastest growing ethnic
groups in the United States,

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:14.160
and they appear to
largely retain their diets,

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:16.560
with about the same
percentage of vegetarians

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:18.926
as in India—nearly 40%.

00:04:18.926 --> 00:04:23.520
We know in India itself,
nonvegetarians (those who eat meat)

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:26.960
are at significantly higher
risk of fatty liver disease.

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:31.440
In Taiwan, you see the same thing:
vegetarians at significantly lower risk.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:33.760
And even the vegetarians
who were affected had

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:36.320
significantly less liver scarring.

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:39.520
Their data suggests that
replacing a single serving of soy

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:42.160
with a serving of meat or
fish was associated with

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:46.240
12% to 13% increased risk
of fatty liver disease.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:49.600
But what about here
in the United States?

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:52.240
Eating vegetarian was
associated with being slimmer,

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:54.320
having better blood sugars,
better cholesterol,

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:59.120
and less than half the
odds of fatty liver disease.

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:01.840
You don’t know if it’s
cause-and-effect, though,

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:05.280
until you... put it to the test.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:08.480
In an effort to reverse
a fatty liver patient’s

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:10.960
inflammatory bowel disease
with a plant-based diet,

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:14.160
liver inflammation was
dramatically improved.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:15.600
But, he also lost about 9 pounds

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:17.760
in the first 11 days
thanks to eating healthy;

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:21.360
so, it’s hard to tease out
the specific diet effects.

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:24.640
In fact, you have to be
careful about rapid weight loss,

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:27.440
because all that extra fat
being broken down can flood

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:29.920
into the blood stream and
sometimes make things worse.

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:32.400
So, for fatty liver disease
patients, losing like

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:35.440
three pounds a week might be safer.

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:38.560
Even though plant-based diets
have yet to be properly

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:40.880
be put to the test in a
randomized clinical trial

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:44.320
for fatty liver disease, I
would submit that they are

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:47.120
still the best diet for fatty liver disease.

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:48.960
Not based on a single case report,

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:51.600
but based on the fact
that cardiovascular disease

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:54.480
is the most common cause
of death among patients

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:57.680
with fatty liver disease (not liver failure).

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:00.080
And we do have randomized
controlled trials

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:02.880
proving that a healthy plant-based
diet and lifestyle program

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:06.560
can reverse heart disease, opening
up arteries without drugs,

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:09.120
without surgery, without stents.

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:12.400
Yes, patients with fatty liver
disease and fatty hepatitis

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:15.520
may indeed eventually develop
cirrhosis of the liver,

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:22.023
but only if they don’t die of
cardiovascular diseases first.

